
# GIT CLONE

## Git Clone

- `git clone` copies a remote repository onto my computer.

- Example:

    git clone https://github.com/user/project.git

- This downloads the repository and creates a local Git repository.

- I can then:

    cd project

- And start working on it.

- This is commonly how I download an existing GitHub project.

---

# GIT FORK

## GitHub Forks

- A fork is my own GitHub copy of someone else's repository.

- Forks are especially useful for open-source projects.

- Example:

    Someone else's repository
            ↓
          Fork
            ↓
    My GitHub repository

- I can make changes to my fork without directly changing the original project.

- I can then create a Pull Request back to the original project.

- This is a common way to contribute to open-source software.

